{"gold":[{"independent_answer":"84000","question_sha256":"c1f0db194571bbc6ef51e6d8089205aef605dbb87d116c942b35cdacf19c56ec","reason":"Four hours is 4 × 60 = 240 minutes per day. At 50 words per minute, Carl types 50 × 240 = 12,000 words per day, and over 7 days he types 12,000 × 7 = 84,000 words. This equals the supplied gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-309"},{"independent_answer":"25","question_sha256":"b6d14deafc2c5fe0e9007cb8ec26e681d6dc486dafcc833ea6f6f2d92ff6b8eb","reason":"The four hoses deliver 2 × 2 + 2 × 3 = 10 gallons per minute. Filling 15,000 gallons takes 15,000 ÷ 10 = 1,500 minutes, or 1,500 ÷ 60 = 25 hours. This equals the supplied gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-5046"},{"independent_answer":"40","question_sha256":"137fd485bceb6a4a5cd77ab6c8a645918d66f712ec7a56d5b236fffc4b19689a","reason":"Five hoses at 20 gallons per minute provide 5 × 20 = 100 gallons per minute. Delivering 4,000 gallons therefore takes 4,000 ÷ 100 = 40 minutes, equal to the supplied gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-5122"},{"independent_answer":"12","question_sha256":"3ba186da02082411d9e3ea2ebf205a0c1cbcd02e78050d288ab9fada7dc01ae3","reason":"Two hours is 2 × 60 = 120 minutes. At one new color every 10 minutes, the sky turns to 120 ÷ 10 = 12 new colors during that duration. This equals the supplied gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-5053"},{"independent_answer":"95","question_sha256":"4a0098f73295b4e685adb0b317a1a4c67059ed0a0278140dafdcccca89d31eaa","reason":"The balloons require 52 × 5 = 260 gallons. Kate fills 10 × 8 = 80 gallons first and then 5 × 4 = 20 gallons at half rate, leaving 260 − 80 − 20 = 160 gallons. The remainder takes 160 ÷ 2 = 80 minutes, so total time is 10 + 5 + 80 = 95 minutes, equal to the supplied gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-5367"},{"independent_answer":"20","question_sha256":"736dd501693d34247f372692980694150a77fe9c99f8bc475650ad07beb97f8c","reason":"From 8 AM to noon is 4 hours. Carla 